WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.880
Under $50 sounds clear.

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:04.440
AI didn’t treat it the same way.

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:08.350
In RecoScope’s November 18 skincare snapshot,

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:10.100
we captured 12 usable answers

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.500
across four assistants and three prompt types.

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:16.500
CeraVe appeared in nine answers and La Roche-Posay in eight.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:19.000
Three comparisons ranked CeraVe first.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.200
Gemini picked La Roche-Posay.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.520
But the budget prompt asked for skincare under $50.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:29.420
ChatGPT, Claude and Gemini described limits per product.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:32.320
Claude’s four listed products total $76.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:36.400
Perplexity explicitly treated $50 as the total,

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:40.500
quoting a three-product basket at $39.97 before tax.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.260
Mention counts don’t tell you whether a recommendation fits the budget.

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:47.000
These findings describe captured answers,

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.320
not product quality or medical advice.

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:52.240
Explore benchmark at getrecoscope.com.

